  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWorkerGlobalScope has a distinct [embedder policy field](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#concept-workerglobalscope-embedder-policy) which is never initialized, only read.\n\nIn [run a worker](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#worker-processing-model:initialize-worker-policy-container), the [policy conatiner](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/workers.html#concept-workerglobalscope-policy-container) for the WorkerGlobalScope is initalized during `processResponseConsumeBody` for the worker's script. Two steps later, the uninitialized embedder policy field is read to perform some CORS checks. \n\n[check a global object's embedder policy](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#check-a-global-object's-embedder-policy), which applies only to WorkerGlobalScope objects, also refers directly to the WorkerGlobalScope's embedder policy, rather than its policy conatiner's embedder policy.\n\nThis feels like a straightforward cleanup? But there might be other places that are half-converted to use policy containers vs many policy fields. ",
